WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:04.920
Riverdale delivers a sexy, updated take on
the classic Archie comics, but what would

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:08.260
it look like if the cast was a little closer
to their comics counterparts?

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:09.980
Jughead Jones

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:15.099
To take on an angsty version of Jughead, Cole
Sprouse dyed his naturally blonde hair to

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.040
dark brown, and he sports the character’s
signature hat, no matter how weird it might

00:00:19.060 --> 00:00:19.560
be.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:23.760
The only thing that keeps him from being a
dead ringer is Jughead’s Pinocchio-style

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:24.260
nose.

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:25.980
Archie Andrews

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.840
Like Kevin Keller said in episode one: Archie
got hot.

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:30.340
K.J.

00:00:30.340 --> 00:00:35.180
Apa's Archie is super-jacked, with red-dyed
hair alongside thick black eyebrows of the

00:00:35.180 --> 00:00:35.680
comics.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.380
He makes viewers believe that Archie Andrews
could be the kind of guy two best friends

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:41.000
would fight over for eighty years.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:45.040
But he's still missing the trademark freckles
and clumsiness of the comics.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:46.660
Betty Cooper

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:51.899
Riverdale’s resident brilliant blonde is
played by Lili Reinhart, who sports Betty’s

00:00:51.900 --> 00:00:54.940
iconic ponytail… when she’s not sporting
a wig as “Dark Betty.”

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:58.719
Reinhart’s hair is a little darker than
the cartoon blonde of the comics, and she

00:00:58.719 --> 00:01:01.329
lacks the bangs that Betty is usually depicted
with.

00:01:01.329 --> 00:01:03.900
Other than that, though, she could’ve stepped
off the page.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:05.600
Veronica Lodge

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:10.660
Brazilian-American actress Camila Mendes said
she wasn’t planning on auditioning for Veronica

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:14.380
until she found out the producers were making
the character Latina, and that she like liked

00:01:14.380 --> 00:01:16.040
that the character “wasn’t a stereotype.”

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:20.659
Aside from the change in background and the
Bettie Page bangs that Veronica has in the

00:01:20.660 --> 00:01:24.400
comics, Mendes is virtually identical to Riverdale’s
richest teenager.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:25.880
Cheryl Blossom

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:31.400
Cheryl Blossom was once banned from Archie
comics for being too sexy, but Madelaine Petsch

00:01:31.409 --> 00:01:36.140
steals the show as the River Vixens’ dramatic
HBIC, whether she’s involved in a murder

00:01:36.140 --> 00:01:38.340
mystery or shooting enemies with arrows.

00:01:38.340 --> 00:01:43.320
Like Cheryl of the comics, Petsch is redheaded,
although her hair's darker than in the comics,

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:45.600
and her brown eyes depart from Cheryl’s
green.

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.060
Kevin Keller

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:52.320
Kevin Keller made headlines in 2010 when he
was introduced as the first openly gay character

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.659
in Archie Comics, and has been a mainstay
of the cast ever since.

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:58.720
Actor Casey Cott's hair is dark brown, along
with green eyes.

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:03.039
Those are both departures from comic book
Kevin Keller, who sports wavy blonde hair,

00:02:03.040 --> 00:02:04.140
and bright blue eyes.

00:02:04.620 --> 00:02:05.840
Ms. Grundy

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:09.459
The character we think is Geraldine Grundy
isn't.

00:02:09.459 --> 00:02:13.410
Jennifer Gibson stole Grundy’s identity
and started an inappropriate relationship

00:02:13.410 --> 00:02:14.840
with 15 year-old Archie.

00:02:14.960 --> 00:02:19.300
34 year-old Sarah Habel is pretty different
from comics-Grundy in every way.

00:02:19.310 --> 00:02:23.519
We eventually see the “real” Ms. Grundy
in the newspaper, looking exactly like her

00:02:23.520 --> 00:02:26.360
comics counterpart, but otherwise, we’re
far from the source here.

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:28.500
Fred Andrews

00:02:28.980 --> 00:02:34.120
On TV, former teen heartthrob Luke Perry sports
a full head of hair and chiseled good looks,

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:36.760
showing exactly where his son Archie gets
his handsomeness.

00:02:36.760 --> 00:02:40.840
That's a stark contrast to comic book Fred
Andrews, who's overweight and nearly bald.

00:02:40.840 --> 00:02:45.540
And it's a good thing, too: a bald, mustachioed
Luke Perry is not the Luke Perry we want.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:47.060
Hiram Lodge

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:52.580
As Hiram Lodge, Mark Consuelos has a sinister
cool, the physique to grapple on the wrestling

00:02:52.580 --> 00:02:55.690
mat, and the edge to intimidate mobsters like
Poppa Poutine.

00:02:55.690 --> 00:02:59.080
But “cool” and “sinister” aren’t
words that could plausibly describe him in

00:02:59.080 --> 00:02:59.680
the comics.

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:04.280
With white hair, a thick mustache, and glasses,
Hiram's a stuffy businessman who tends to

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:05.800
fall into swimming pools.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:07.180
Toni Topaz

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:12.050
Toni Topaz was introduced into the comics
as a potential love interest for Jughead,

00:03:12.050 --> 00:03:15.900
which meant she was a competitive eater who
crushed the competition at a cupcake-eating

00:03:15.900 --> 00:03:16.400
contest.

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:20.720
On the show, Vanessa Morgan's ability to scarf
down desserts has yet to be fully explored,

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:24.540
but beyond that, she bears a pretty strong
resemblance to her comics counterpart.

00:03:24.960 --> 00:03:25.840
Penny Peabody

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:30.840
Penny Peabody is definitely the most obscure
character to make it to the screen, originally

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:33.380
appearing as a child in the Little Archie
spinoff.

00:03:33.740 --> 00:03:38.400
Brit Morgan brings her to TV as a ruthless
attorney working for the Southside Serpents,

00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:42.450
and given what happens between her and Jughead,
it’s probably for the best that Riverdale

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:43.980
made her a much older woman.

00:03:44.460 --> 00:03:45.800
Nick St. Clair

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:50.200
Unlike most characters on Riverdale, Nick
St. Clair wasn't originally designed for the

00:03:50.200 --> 00:03:53.159
cartoony style that we all recognize from
Archie Comics.

00:03:53.159 --> 00:03:55.909
Instead, he was introduced as a modern "bad
boy."

00:03:55.909 --> 00:04:01.140
Graham Phillips lacks the spiky hair and soul
patch from the comics, but otherwise, he absolutely

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:04.640
plays Nick with the same smug smarminess that
makes him so hateable.

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:06.360
The Red Circle

00:04:06.780 --> 00:04:12.060
In the comics, "Red Circle" a line of superhero
comics featuring characters like the Shield,

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:13.480
Jaguar, and Fly Girl.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:18.240
Riverdale transformed that idea by having
Archie get inspired to form a vigilante gang

00:04:18.240 --> 00:04:21.440
of masked, shirtless teens after reading too
many funnybooks.

00:04:21.590 --> 00:04:25.300
The only thing that would’ve made it weirder
is if Archie actually started fighting crime

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:25.900
as the Shield.

